_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":1.5,"_gate_roic_consistency":1.2660892180714824,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.046915038571105606,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":1.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.15641827746205328,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":-0.07077305717566262,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":11.7,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.051046639623704884,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":67.8,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.000726883114094079,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":50.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":100.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.024149999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":16.1,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Newmark Group, Inc. operates as a commercial real estate advisor and service provider in the United States, the United Kingdom, Asia, rest of Europe, and other Americas. The company offers capital markets services consisting of investment sales, including placement and raising of equity; and commercial mortgage brokerage, such as government-sponsored enterprises (GSEs) and federal housing administration (FHA) lending, as well as the placement of debt, loan sales, and structured finance on behalf of third parties. It also provides landlord or agency representation leasing; GSEs and FHA multifamily loan servicing, as well as limited loan servicing, special loan servicing, and asset management; management consulting, managed services, and fund accounting for investors; valuation and advisory services; property management and workspace solutions for owners; due diligence, consulting, and other advisory services; commercial real estate technology platform and capabilities; and business rates for property owners. In addition, the company offers tenant representation leasing; occupier solutions comprising project management, transaction management, lease administration, and facilities management, as well as corporate consulting services to real estate and supply chain optimization, workplace strategy, and occupancy strategy areas; workspace solutions for occupiers; and business rates for occupiers. It serves commercial real estate tenants, investors, owners, occupiers, and developers, lenders, small and medium size businesses, multi-national corporations, and institutional owners of real estate. The company was formerly known as Newmark Grubb Knight Frank Capital Group and changed its name to Newmark Group, Inc. in October 2017. Newmark Group, Inc. was founded in 1929 and is based in New York, New York. Newmark Group, Inc. operates as a subsidiary of Cantor Fitzgerald, L.P.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Barry M. Gosin | Chief Executive Officer | Age 74 | Compensation: $2.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 10K people. Revenue per employee of $314K ranks in the bottom quartile among Real Estate peers, improving at 7%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $14K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Newmark Group, Inc. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $2.9B market cap on $3.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $143M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.36\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 4.2\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.4% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.3pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 16% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 18% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 32% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Financial quality scores above most Real Estate peers","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Earnings Beat Might Change The Case For Investing In Newmark Group Stock (NMRK)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate-management-and-development/nasdaq-nmrk/newmark-group/news/earnings-beat-might-change-the-case-for-investing-in-newmark","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793770862.707,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.796,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"(NMRK) as a Liquidity Pulse for Institutional Tactics","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/81/NMRK_as_a_Liquidity_Pulse_for_Institutional_Tactics_110226054402_1793659442.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793659442.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Newmark Group (NMRK) A Bargain After Its Strong Q3 Earnings?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate-management-and-development/nasdaq-nmrk/newmark-group/news/is-newmark-group-nmrk-a-bargain-after-its-strong-q3-earnings","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793658042.947,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.735,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Vanguard Portfolio Management Reports 9.82% Stake in Newmark Group Inc (NASDAQ:NMRK)","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/vanguard-portfolio-management-reports-982-stake-in-newmark-group-inc-nasdaqnmrk","date":"2026-10-30","timestamp"